<title>UK: TABLE-TI H1 profits at top of forecasts.</title>
<headline>TABLE-TI H1 profits at top of forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.1		   vs 19.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.10		   vs 4.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     112.1		  vs 125.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   933		    vs 895</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 108-112 million stg, compared to 103.7 million stg last year before exceptional gains on disposals of 21.6 million stg.</p>
<p>The company also said it was paying its dividind this year as a Foreign Income Dividend to save tax, which would result in a cash saving of five million stg for the full year.</p>
<p>Full company name - TI Group Plc</p>
</text>
